    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0747" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2834</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poole</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">temporarily at Christiania, to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-28T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 29, 5.33
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have come here with a view to accelerating if possible through the Norwegian
                    Government departure from Russia of the Americans <pb facs="0748" n="674"
                        xml:id="pg674"/> mentioned my No. 9 of the 25th. Will return Stockholm
                    October 1. Norwegian Chargé d’Affaires, Petrograd, also here, having left
                    Petrograd 25th. He reports that special messenger has been sent to Tsaritsyn to
                    bring Vice Consuls Burri and Leonard to Moscow and that Chicherin has given
                    written order for their departure from Russia. Chicherin also promises that Paul
                    Anderson will be released and permitted to depart. I am telegraphing Wardwell of
                    the Red Cross to hasten in every way his and Andrews’s leaving.</p>
                <p>Norwegian Chargé d’Affaires reports conditions unchanged at Petrograd on the day
                    of the departure, wholesale arrests continuing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
